{"call_id": "7eb82c1265724cd2846a9c439467b144", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/quickcheck/runs/natural/stockindex/query2/quick-01/results/7eb82c1265724cd2846a9c439467b144.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"TASK: Among North American stock indices, which indices had more up days than down days in 2018?\\n\\nANSWER: Only the NASDAQ Composite (index symbol: IXIC).\\n\\nREASONING:\\n- The index_info database lists 14 exchanges; the North American ones are the New York Stock Exchange (USD), NASDAQ (USD), and Toronto Stock Exchange (CAD).\\n- The corresponding indices in the index_trade database are: NYA (NYSE Composite), IXIC (NASDAQ Composite), and GSPTSE (S&P/TSX Composite).\\n- An \\\"up day\\\" is a trading day where Close > Open, and a \\\"down day\\\" where Close < Open. All 2018 trading days were analyzed (mixed date formats parsed and verified to fall in year 2018; 251 trading days each).\\n\\nResults for 2018:\\n- IXIC (NASDAQ Composite): 131 up days vs 120 down days -> MORE UP DAYS THAN DOWN DAYS\\n- NYA (NYSE Composite): 125 up days vs 126 down days -> no\\n- GSPTSE (S&P/TSX Composite, Toronto): 115 up days vs 135 down days (1 flat day) -> no\\n\\nTherefore, the only North American stock index with more up days than down days in 2018 was the NASDAQ Composite (IXIC).\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
